I'm still unsure whether we should add support for the URI scheme `mongo+srv` or just disable the setting except in engineering mode.
@sulkaharo Do I understand you correctly that the new URI scheme is just not supported but still possible?
Are there any differences between `mongo` and `mongo+srv`.

@sulkaharo I'm trying to upload a document to a new collection in nightscout but my code fails with error 404

Here is the code that I'm trying:

url = 'https://snirdar3.herokuapp.com/api/v1/libre'
payload = {'some': 'data'}
payload = {"_id":"5fd370324e412324f4d253a5","device":"xDrip-LimiTTerWifi","date":1607692311331,"dateString":"2020-12-11T13:11:51.331Z","sgv":134,"delta":-12.55,"direction":"SingleDown","type":"sgv","filtered":131176.46075,"unfiltered":131176.46075,"rssi":100,"noise":1,"sysTime":"2020-12-11T13:11:51.331Z","utcOffset":120,"mills":1607692311331}
headers = {'content-type': 'application/json',
           'api-secret': 'xxx'}

response = requests.post(url, data=json.dumps(payload), headers=headers)
print(response, response.content)

If I upload the same data to the entries collection this works. So, I wonder if nightscout only supports uploading to a fixed set of collections.
